@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+/* ── THE COMMIT LEG — the material's answer to a model change (D5-D) ──────────────
+   A substrate that carries state writes `--commit-t` 0 at one state and 1 at the
+   other, and lists `--commit-t` in its own transition on `--spring-panel`. The
+   phase travels 0 → 1 (or back) and overshoots by the panel spring's own rebound;
+   the host's `transform` reads it as one swell and one dip:
+
+       scale = 1 + amp · sin(π · t)       t = 0 and t = 1 both rest at scale 1
+
+   A transition, not an animation: a host mounted in its committed state has no
+   prior style, so nothing starts (H-8). A model change with no gesture moves the
+   attribute and the phase alike, so keyboard, programmatic and pointer commits
+   take one path. `--commit-amp` is each substrate's, read off the press table so
+   the swell mirrors the squish; reduce zeroes it (the state still lands). */
+@property --commit-t {
+    syntax: "<number>";
+    inherits: false;
+    initial-value: 0;
+}
+
+@layer components {
+    :is(.control-bit, .disclosure-trigger) {
+        transform: scale(calc(1 + var(--commit-amp, 0) * sin(var(--commit-t) * 180deg)));
+    }
+
+    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
+        :is(.control-bit, .disclosure-trigger) {
+            --commit-amp: 0;
+        }
+    }
+}
